{
  "key": "irrealis_constructions",
  "concept_slug": "irrealis_constructions",
  "grounding_mode": "fallback_no_wiki",
  "title": "Hypothetical and Unreal Conditions",
  "cefr_level": "B2",
  "goal": "Build and recognize Norwegian sentences about hypothetical or contrary-to-fact situations.",
  "objectives": [
    {
      "id": "obj_clause_condition",
      "statement": "Use hvis, dersom, and om to introduce hypothetical condition clauses.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obj_modal_result",
      "statement": "Use ville, skulle, and hadde to express unreal or tentative meaning without a special subjunctive form.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obj_inversion",
      "statement": "Recognize and form natural inverted conditionals such as Hadde jeg tid.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obj_diagnose",
      "statement": "Diagnose common English-transfer errors in Norwegian irrealis sentences.",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "understand"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_000",
      "role": "orient",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_clause_condition",
        "obj_modal_result"
      ],
      "title": "What Irrealis Means",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Irrealis means that you are not presenting something as a plain fact. You may be imagining it, making it dependent on a condition, or saying that it is contrary to reality."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Norwegian normally does this with clause structure and modal verbs. A modal verb changes the meaning of another verb, such as "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ville",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "skulle",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". Modern Bokmål does not have a productive subjunctive form that you add to ordinary verbs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "For most hypothetical sentences, put the condition in a clause with "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hvis",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "dersom",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "om",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", and put the imagined result in a main clause."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hvis jeg hadde mer tid, ville jeg lære samisk."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "If I had more time, I would learn Sami."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Dersom prisen var lavere, ville flere kjøpe billetter."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "If the price were lower, more people would buy tickets."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_001",
      "role": "model",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_clause_condition"
      ],
      "title": "If Clauses",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Hvis",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " is the most general word for if. "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Dersom",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " is a little more formal or careful. "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Om",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " can also mean if, especially in open or tentative conditions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "A subordinate clause is a dependent clause introduced by a word like "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hvis",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". When it comes first, the finite verb comes immediately after the comma in the main clause."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "When the if clause comes first, use verb-second order in the result: condition comma finite verb subject."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Om du trengte mer informasjon, kunne jeg sende rapporten."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "If you needed more information, I could send the report."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hvis møtet startet tidligere, ville vi rekke toget."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "If the meeting started earlier, we would catch the train."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "warning",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Do not copy English word order after a fronted if clause. "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "Hvis jeg hadde tid, jeg ville komme",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " is not natural Bokmål. Use "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "ville jeg komme",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_002",
      "role": "contrast",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_modal_result"
      ],
      "title": "The Modal Verbs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Norwegian often uses the simple past, called preteritum in Norwegian grammar, to make a situation less direct, less real, or contrary to fact. This is why you see forms like "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hadde",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "var",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ville",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", and "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "skulle",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " even when the imagined situation is about now or the future."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "col_langs": [
            "en",
            "no",
            "en"
          ],
          "headers": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Meaning"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Form"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Use"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "would"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "ville"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "imagined result or willingness"
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "were to, should"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "skulle"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "tentative condition or planned action"
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "had"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "hadde"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "unreal possession or circumstance"
                }
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg ville sagt ja, men datoen passer ikke."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I would say yes, but the date does not work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Skulle du få problemer, kan du ringe meg."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "If you should have problems, you can call me."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "note",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "This lesson keeps to present or future hypothetical meaning. Sentences about unreal past results use another pattern with "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "ha",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " plus a past participle."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_003",
      "role": "contrast",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_inversion"
      ],
      "title": "Inverted Conditions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Norwegian can make a condition without "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hvis",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " by starting with the finite verb. This is called inversion, the verb comes before the subject."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "In an inverted conditional, start with the finite verb: "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Hadde jeg tid",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", not "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Jeg hadde tid",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hadde jeg bedre råd, ville jeg bodd nærmere sentrum."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "If I could afford it, I would live closer to the city center."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Skulle planen endre seg, gir jeg beskjed."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "If the plan should change, I will let you know."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "This construction is common in writing and careful speech. In everyday speech, a sentence with "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hvis",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " is often simpler and just as correct."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_004",
      "role": "recap",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_clause_condition",
        "obj_modal_result",
        "obj_inversion",
        "obj_diagnose"
      ],
      "title": "Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "To sound natural in hypothetical Norwegian, build the sentence through condition markers, modal verbs, and word order rather than through a special subjunctive ending."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Use "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "hvis",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "dersom",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", or "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "om",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for explicit if clauses."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Use simple past forms such as "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "hadde",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and modal forms such as "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "ville",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for unreal or imagined meaning."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Use inverted conditions like "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "Hadde jeg tid",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " when you want a concise written style."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "After a fronted condition, keep Norwegian verb-second order in the result clause."
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
